[38;5;231m⏺[39m That adds a date range, which the guidelines already cover. 03-forms says a date range is two date pickers at [38;5;153msm[39m width
  each, start before end, with a presets Select beside them. Invalid order shows the catalog message "The end date must
  be after the start date." So the bar will have the event select, From and To dates with a presets Select, and search.
  Dates use your local time zone, matching how the When column already displays.

  The next question is about security changes. A single event-type Select picks only one type, but "anything that
  changed my security settings" covers several. I see three ways to handle it:

  - [1mGrouped Select with a combined option:[0m add an "All security changes" option near the top, and group the nine types
    into "Sign-ins" and "Account changes" (03 says to group long lists). It stays one control, matches option A, and
    adds little code. It rules out arbitrary combinations, such as failed sign-ins plus password changes together.
  - [1mCheckbox list instead of a Select:[0m pick any mix. That's a fieldset of nine checkboxes, which makes the bar much
    taller, moves away from the layout you picked, and adds more code.

  I recommend the [1mgrouped Select with "All security changes"[0m. It covers both of the common searches in one choice each.

  If you agree, please confirm which types count as security changes. I'd include [1mPassword changed, Two-factor enabled,
[0m  [1mand Email change requested[0m. "Settings updated" is generic, so should it count, or stay out?

